cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MoE-Direct or its measurement methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "MoE-Direct: Byte-preserving MoE expert streaming from NVMe on consumer hardware"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "tmxkzm1925-max"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tmxkzm1925-max/moe-direct"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-07-26
version: "0.1-project-preview"
abstract: >-
  MoE-Direct serves Mixture-of-Experts LLMs whose weights exceed system memory
  by keeping repacked, 4KiB-aligned expert records on NVMe and reading them on
  demand into a deterministic slot cache, with SHA-verified byte-equal expert
  records, token-ID parity verified under deterministic greedy OFF/ON
  protocols, asynchronous queue-depth I/O, and a counterfactual replay
  methodology for validating expert prefetch before implementation. Measured
  on a 32GB RAM / 16GB VRAM Windows PC: Qwen3.5-122B (72.3GiB GGUF) at
  5.14 tok/s mean decode (non-gating measured mean); a 1T-class model
  (416.8GiB GGUF, Q3_K experts) produced coherent output at 1.03 tok/s in a
  non-gating run.
